Sure thing! I’ll add a running subtotal to the cart page and make sure it’s carried over to the checkout step.

**What I’ll do**

1. **cart.html** – add a place to show the subtotal.  
2. **script.js** – extend the cart‑logic to total up all line‑item prices and update the new subtotal field whenever items are added/removed.  
3. **app.py** – (optional) expose the subtotal in the JSON response if you’re rendering the cart server‑side, but the client‑side script already does the math, so you can keep the backend unchanged.

---

### 1. cart.html – add a subtotal row

Find the `<table id="cart-table">` (or wherever you list the items) and insert a footer row right after the list of items:

```html
<table id="cart-table">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Product</th>
      <th>Qty</th>
      <th>Price</th>
      <th>Total</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody id="cart-items">
    <!-- rows get injected by script.js -->
  </tbody>
  <tfoot>
    <tr>
      <td colspan="3" style="text-align:right;font-weight:bold;">Subtotal:</td>
      <td id="cart-subtotal">$0.00</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td colspan="4" style="text-align:center;">
        <button id="checkout-btn">Proceed to Checkout</button>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tfoot>
</table>
```

The `<td id="cart-subtotal">` will be updated by JavaScript.

---

### 2. script.js – calculate & display the subtotal

Add a helper function and call it whenever the cart changes:

```js
// existing code that adds/removes items ...

function formatCurrency(num) {
  return '$' + num.toFixed(2);
}

// ---- NEW: subtotal calculation ----
function updateSubtotal() {
  const rows = document.querySelectorAll('#cart-items tr');
  let sum = 0;
  rows.forEach(row => {
    const totalCell = row.querySelector('.item-total'); // assuming you have this class
    if (totalCell) {
      const amount = parseFloat(totalCell.textContent.replace('$','')) || 0;
      sum += amount;
    }
  });
  document.getElementById('cart-subtotal').textContent = formatCurrency(sum);
}

// Call updateSubtotal() after any add/remove/quantity change
// Example: after you rebuild the cart UI
function renderCart(items) {
  const tbody = document.getElementById('cart-items');
  tbody.innerHTML = '';
  items.forEach(item => {
    const tr = document.createElement('tr');
    tr.innerHTML = `
      <td>${item.name}</td>
      <td><input type="number" min="1" value="${item.qty}" class="qty-input" data-id="${item.id}"></td>
      <td class="item-price">${formatCurrency(item.price)}</td>
      <td class="item-total">${formatCurrency(item.price * item.qty)}</td>
      <td><button class="remove-btn" data-id="${item.id}">✕</button></td>
    `;
    tbody.appendChild(tr);
  });
  // after rebuilding the rows, recalc subtotal
  updateSubtotal();
}

// Hook qty changes & remove button to re‑render
document.addEventListener('click', e => {
  if (e.target.matches('.remove-btn')) {
    // remove logic …
    renderCart(updatedItems);
  }
});

document.addEventListener('change', e => {
  if (e.target.matches('.qty-input')) {
    // qty change logic …
    renderCart(updatedItems);
  }
});
```

If you already have a `renderCart` (or similar) function, just inject the `updateSubtotal()` call at the end. The key is that every time the DOM representation of the cart changes, you recompute the sum and write it to `#cart-subtotal`.

---

### 3. (Optional) Pass subtotal to the server on checkout

If your checkout endpoint expects the total amount, you can send it along with the cart payload:

```js
document.getElementById('checkout-btn').addEventListener('click', () => {
  const subtotalText = document.getElementById('cart-subtotal').textContent;
  const subtotal = parseFloat(subtotalText.replace('$',''));

  fetch('/checkout', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ items: currentCartItems, subtotal })
  })
  .then(res => res.json())
  .then(data => {
    // handle order confirmation …
  });
});
```

No changes are required in `app.py` unless you want to validate the subtotal server‑side; in that case just read `request.json['subtotal']`.

---

That’s it! Drop the updated snippets into the respective files, refresh the page, and you’ll see the subtotal automatically update as users modify their cart and when they hit “Proceed to Checkout.” Let me know if you run into any hiccups or need the checkout page itself to display the subtotal as well. Happy coding!

Here are the exact changes you need to make. Just replace the highlighted sections in the existing files with the code below.

**1. cart.html – add a place to show the subtotal**

Locate the main `<div class="cart-container">` (or wherever the cart table is) and insert the following line right after the table (or at the bottom of the cart section):

```html
<div class="cart-subtotal" style="margin-top:1rem; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.2rem;">
    Subtotal: $<span id="cart-subtotal">0.00</span>
</div>
```

If you already have a “total” row, you can replace it with the snippet above – the script will fill in the value dynamically.

**2. script.js – calculate and display the running subtotal**

Find the part of the script that renders the cart items (usually a function called `renderCart()` or similar). After you finish building the HTML for each line‑item, add the subtotal calculation and update the new `<span>`.

Replace or add the following code inside your cart‑rendering logic:

```javascript
function renderCart() {
    const cart = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('cart')) || [];
    const cartTableBody = document.getElementById('cart-items');
    cartTableBody.innerHTML = '';
    let subtotal = 0;

    cart.forEach((item, index) => {
        const row = document.createElement('tr');

        // ----- existing columns (image, name, price, qty, remove) -----
        // example:
        const nameCell = document.createElement('td');
        nameCell.textContent = item.name;
        row.appendChild(nameCell);

        const priceCell = document.createElement('td');
        priceCell.textContent = `$${item.price.toFixed(2)}`;
        row.appendChild(priceCell);

        const qtyCell = document.createElement('td');
        const qtyInput = document.createElement('input');
        qtyInput.type = 'number';
        qtyInput.min = 1;
        qtyInput.value = item.quantity;
        qtyInput.addEventListener('change', (e) => {
            const newQty = parseInt(e.target.value, 10);
            if (newQty > 0) {
                item.quantity = newQty;
                saveCart(cart);
                renderCart();            // re‑render to refresh subtotal
            }
        });
        qtyCell.appendChild(qtyInput);
        row.appendChild(qtyCell);
        // --------------------------------------------------------------

        // calculate line‑total and add to subtotal
        const lineTotal = item.price * item.quantity;
        subtotal += lineTotal;

        // optional: show line‑total column
        const lineTotalCell = document.createElement('td');
        lineTotalCell.textContent = `$${lineTotal.toFixed(2)}`;
        row.appendChild(lineTotalCell);

        // remove button (if you have one)
        const removeCell = document.createElement('td');
        const removeBtn = document.createElement('button');
        removeBtn.textContent = 'Remove';
        removeBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
            cart.splice(index, 1);
            saveCart(cart);
            renderCart();
        });
        removeCell.appendChild(removeBtn);
        row.appendChild(removeCell);

        cartTableBody.appendChild(row);
    });

    // ---- update the subtotal display ----
    document.getElementById('cart-subtotal').textContent = subtotal.toFixed(2);
}
```

If your script already has a `saveCart()` helper, keep using it; otherwise add this tiny utility:

```javascript
function saveCart(cart) {
    localStorage.setItem('cart', JSON.stringify(cart));
}
```

**3. Pass the subtotal to the checkout page (optional)**

If you move from `cart.html` to a separate checkout page (e.g., `checkout.html`), you can store the subtotal in `sessionStorage` right before navigation:

```javascript
document.getElementById('checkout-button').addEventListener('click', () => {
    const subtotal = parseFloat(document.getElementById('cart-subtotal').textContent);
    sessionStorage.setItem('checkout-subtotal', subtotal.toFixed(2));
    window.location.href = 'checkout.html';
});
```

Then on `checkout.html` you can display it with:

```html
<p>Order Subtotal: $<span id="checkout-subtotal"></span></p>
<script>
    const sub = sessionStorage.getItem('checkout-subtotal') || '0.00';
    document.getElementById('checkout-subtotal').textContent = sub;
</script>
```

**4. Refresh the cart on page load**

Make sure you call `renderCart()` when the cart page loads:

```javascript
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', renderCart);
```

---

### Quick test checklist

1. Add a product to the cart → the subtotal at the bottom should update instantly.  
2. Change the quantity of any line item → subtotal recalculates automatically.  
3. Remove an item → subtotal drops accordingly.  
4. Click the “Checkout” button → subtotal value is stored in `sessionStorage` and shown on the checkout page.

That’s all you need for a live running subtotal during checkout. Let me know if you hit any snags or need the checkout page wired up further!

