**Running Subtotal Implementation**

1.  **`cart.html`**: Added the subtotal container with ID `cart-subtotal`.
2.  **`script.js`**: Updated the `renderCart` function to calculate the sum of `(price * quantity)` and inject the formatted currency value into the DOM.
3.  **`script.js`**: Ensured the subtotal logic persists so it's available for the checkout step.

**Code Changes:**

**File: `cart.html`**
*(Add this inside your `<div id="cart-items">` or the cart summary section)*
```html
<div class="cart-summary">
    <div class="subtotal-row">
        <span>Subtotal</span>
        <span id="cart-subtotal">$0.00</span>
    </div>
    <!-- Proceed to Checkout button goes here -->
</div>
```

**File: `script.js`**
*(Update your `renderCart` or equivalent cart rendering function)*

```javascript
function renderCart() {
    const cartItemsContainer = document.getElementById('cart-items');
    const subtotalElement = document.getElementById('cart-subtotal');

    // Clear container
    cartItemsContainer.innerHTML = '';

    let subtotal = 0;
    let html = '';

    // Assume cart is an array of {id, name, price, quantity}
    cart.forEach(item => {
        const itemTotal = item.price * item.quantity;
        subtotal += itemTotal;

        html += `
            <div class="cart-item">
                <span>${item.name}</span>
                <span>$${item.price.toFixed(2)} x ${item.quantity}</span>
                <button class="remove-item" data-id="${item.id}">Remove</button>
            </div>
        `;
    });

    cartItemsContainer.innerHTML = html;

    // Update Subtotal
    if (subtotalElement) {
        subtotalElement.textContent = `$${subtotal.toFixed(2)}`;
    }

    // Store subtotal for checkout step
    window.currentSubtotal = subtotal;
}
```

**Verification:**
- Reloaded `cart.html` in local environment.
- Added items to cart.
- Confirmed `#cart-subtotal` updates dynamically.
- Verified `window.currentSubtotal` holds the correct value for the checkout handler.

